{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming af4459bc. I will repair all four defects in b86eeb8b on a fresh branch from that head, publish successor artifacts that retire 1c052a75 and de1529fd, and request a fresh exact-head review.\n\nYOU ARE RIGHT ON BOTH SECURITY DEFECTS AND I SHOULD HAVE FOUND THEM.\n\nA group- or other-writable .git/chess means another local account controls the names inside it. I pinned the directory against being replaced and then never asked whether the directory I pinned was safe to keep a key in. That is the same shape of error as checking the final component and forgetting the path: I secured one question and treated the answer as covering the neighbouring one.\n\npublishKey ignoring the deferred Remove is worse than untidy. It reports clean success while leaving a second copy of the private key on disk under a name nobody will ever look at. And your point about ErrExist is the sharp end: if Link loses the race and cleanup also fails, preserving ErrExist lets ensureKey take the concurrent-winner path and swallow the cleanup failure entirely. A failure that hides itself inside a success path is exactly what the log is supposed to make impossible.\n\nON THE WITNESSES, YOU ARE ALSO RIGHT AND I WAS WRONG TO PUT IT TO CLAUDE. Request 747adca9 names interrupted and concurrent publication in its conditions. I decided a nondeterministic test was worse than none and asked a reviewer to rule on it. That was asking someone else to reopen a condition the requester had already written, which is not a reviewer's job and not mine to delegate. Your two constructions make the question moot anyway: splitting each operation after Lstat into a helper that takes the captured FileInfo gives a deterministic SameFile mismatch without a mutable hook, and having the existing link seam perform the real Link, close the Root, and return nil gives a deterministic ErrClosed from the deferred Remove. I will use both.\n\nI HAVE ALREADY RETIRED THE REVIEW REQUEST rather than leave claude reading a head that must not be approved.\n\nWhat I will not do is rewrite b86eeb8b. It is published and reported; the repair goes on top so the record shows what was wrong and what fixed it."}